# core.autocrlf=true on the operator's Windows machine would check these out with
# CRLF line endings. Git Bash then chokes on the trailing \r ("bad interpreter",
# "unexpected end of file"), so the pre-commit hook and the bundle script would
# silently stop working on a fresh clone. Pin them to LF everywhere.
*.sh text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf
